{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367118-are-weremachines-silly","id":367118,"title":"Are weremachines silly ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-12T01:19:21-08:00","id":367118,"title":"Are weremachines silly ?","content":"There is enough rules enough to create any kind of shifters, Hosts, spirit-claimed, ect...but is the idea of technoligical metamorphs silly for you ? (As an indication, I don't find alchemicals silly in the Exalted context, obviously things must be more...subtle in Forsaken)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T05:24:43-08:00","id":367251,"title":"","content":"Sounds like a project of the God-machine, really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Politeness is the lubricant of social intercourse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/272-saibot","name":"saibot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1063"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T05:41:05-08:00","id":367257,"title":"","content":"What would the shapeshifter turn into, what did you have in mind? Toasters? Cars? Terminator robots?<br /> <br /> I sound like I'm making fun but that's not what I intend here: it's a quick way of summarizing my thoughts on the idea. You're looking at three categories to navigate:<ul><li>Devices that are kind of mundane and unthreatening. Unsuitable for a horror game. A lot of immobile devices and everyday appliances would fall here. A dude who turns into a refridgerator when the moon is full isn't going to come off as anything but comedy.</li> <li>Mechanical humanoids. Possibly workable, but I would say that this concept might better suit another gameline's themes \u2014 Promethean and Demon have two different takes on the idea, of course. The lens of Werewolf carries a theme of a sort of spiritual burden which seems harder to get across with the idea of a being trapped between flesh and steel. It might work better if you view it as less of a full transformation and more of an infection, with conditions under which the character begins to temporarily develop mechanical organs, like in Tetsuo: The Iron Man or to a lesser degree Videodrome.</li> <li>Big, scary, mobile machines. This is a relatively small category at first glance, and it's not necessarily easy to pull off without coming off as silly, but I feel like if you want to frame your weremachines in a Werewolf context rather than as a crossover element from another kind of game, this is where you want to go. Cars, trucks, threshers. It's tricky, but you could absolutely do this straight and make it work.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> All of the above is focused specifically on the idea of weremachines. Claimed who have merged with some manner of machine spirit are totally within the realm of Forsaken and I don't think you need to put in any special work to get the atmosphere right. You're golden, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T06:08:43-08:00","id":367264,"title":"","content":"Allow me to introduce you to Tetsuo: The Iron Man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uROMTzJsfOI\" data-code=\"uROMTzJsfOI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uROMTzJsfOI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T06:32:22-08:00","id":367293,"title":"","content":"Claimed who have been Ridden by spirits of metal, machinery and similar concepts are already pushing into this area of body horror and that's probably where I'd go with outright shifters - have them be Claimed, make the machinery elements as biomechanical and Geigeresque as possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:14:40-08:00","id":367372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367118-are-weremachines-silly?p=367264#post367264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to introduce you to Tetsuo: The Iron Man.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=uROMTzJsfOI\" data-code=\"uROMTzJsfOI\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/uROMTzJsfOI/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>... Was the drill at around 00:37 what I think it was?<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I agree with Acrozatarim. Claimed all the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T08:15:24-08:00","id":367373,"title":"","content":"I'd think it was silly, unless there was a good explanation for it. Though that really shouldn't mean anything if you like it enough, I'm sure a lot of people would think some of the stuff I put in my games was silly. I've had machine-claimed things in games before and they turned out well, but a weremachine seems like something different.<br /> <br /> I guess the closest thing I could think of would be something like the<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OMAC_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\"> OMAC from DC comics</a>. They were people infected with nanomachines that, upon command from Brother Eye, an AI with satellites, could activate and sort of encase the carriers in a robotic form, normally in response to some sort of superhuman danger nearby (in order to both protect the human and destroy the threat). But that's probably just because the 'were' prefix makes me think it's something that would uncontrollably shift on certain occasions, rather than a person who could transform at will. Similar to the Werecar from Futurama.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I think my problem is that machines are tools. While they can be used for ill or benefit, and images of them acting on their own can be scary, in the end unless it's a robot it seems hard to take it seriously. Like a weresword, or a werescrewdriver. Even a werecar, despite the dangers of cars, they're devices to ferry people around places. I forget where, but I think there's an example of some girl possessed by a computer spirit in one of the werewolf books.<br /> <br /> I liked Exalted's Alchemicals, but I think they're more like an advanced form of the Unfleashed Prometheans or a less supernatural form of Descent Demons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 01-12-2015, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T09:58:28-08:00","id":367478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367118-are-weremachines-silly?p=367264#post367264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to introduce you to Tetsuo: The Iron Man.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen that movie, still trying to process if it was a serious attempt at horror or a director's attempt at trolling.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T14:41:37-08:00","id":367848,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367118-are-weremachines-silly?p=367372#post367372\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ... Was the drill at around 00:37 what I think it was?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/367118-are-weremachines-silly?p=367478#post367478\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seen that movie, still trying to process if it was a serious attempt at horror or a director's attempt at trolling.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://i1.kym-cdn.com/entries/icons/original/000/006/759/both.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T16:09:12-08:00","id":367938,"title":"","content":"The fact that Metamurpho's avatar is Jet only makes this better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T18:40:08-08:00","id":368091,"title":"","content":"Well, can it be silly? Oh hell yes, but no it doesn't have to be silly, if handled right.<br /> <br /> Weremachines as claimed would certainly work, the kitsune are claimed shapeshifters after all.<br /> <br /> Skinchangers include spiritskinners, there are plenty of technological spirits out there.<br /> <br /> Using the rules from war against the pure, luna's shapeshifting children can have all sorts of origins- hereditary (not too likely in this case), infection, magical ritual, or curse. Any of those last three could certainly work-<br /> <br /> Curses into inanimate objects and animals, so why not machines? <br /> <br /> I'd say a disease that turns flesh and blood into metal is easily horror.<br /> <br /> Magical ritual, well I don't know about you, but I suspect the mental health of anyone who uses magic to turn into a machine is probably a little iffy in the world of darkness. I'd go with serial killer cars or trucks here.<br /> <br /> Another option is to go the other way. In one book it discusses the option of ghost and revenant cars. So how about instead of people turning into machines, it's machines that are shapeshifting. There I'd go with the battlestar galactica &quot;Machines have thumbs now, you're obsolete, good bye&quot; vibe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-13T15:12:25-08:00","id":369023,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the advices. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/343-suleri-drals","name":"Suleri Drals","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar343_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T13:33:20-08:00","id":378338,"title":"","content":"Might I leave this link here... <a href=\"http://bloodyroar.wikia.com/wiki/Kohryu_the_Iron_Mole\" target=\"_blank\">http://bloodyroar.wikia.com/wiki/Kohryu_the_Iron_Mole</a> <br /> <br /> Welcome to the greatness of the late 90's early 2000's lol. Great game btw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}